       <name slugifiedName="name-the-definition-of-audio/l16">The definition of Audio/L16</name>
       <t indent="0" pn="section-3-1">Audio/L16 is based on the well know audio format &quot;L16&quot; described in
 RFC 1890 section 4.4.8 for use with RTP transport.  L16 denotes
-uncompressed audio data, using 16-bit signed representation in twos-
-complement notation and network byte order.  (From section 4.4.8 of
+uncompressed audio data, using 16-bit signed representation in twos-complement notation and network byte order.  (From section 4.4.8 of
 RFC 1890)</t>
       <t indent="0" pn="section-3-2">It may be parametrized by varying the sample rate and the number of
 channels; the parameters are given on the MIME type header.</t>
