+        <dd pn="section-4-2.2">rate: number of samples per second -- Permissible values for
+rate are 8000, 11025, 16000, 22050, 24000, 32000, 44100, and
+48000 samples per second.</dd>
+        <dt pn="section-4-2.3">Optional parameters</dt>
+        <dd pn="section-4-2.4">channels: how many audio streams are interleaved -- defaults
+to 1; stereo would be 2, etc.  Interleaving takes place
+between individual two-byte samples.</dd>
+        <dt pn="section-4-2.5">Encoding considerations</dt>
+        <dd pn="section-4-2.6">Audio data is binary data, and must be encoded for non-binary
+transport; the Base64 encoding is suitable for Email.  Note
+that audio data does not compress easily using lossless
+compression.</dd>
+        <dt pn="section-4-2.7">Security considerations</dt>
+        <dd pn="section-4-2.8">Audio data is believed to offer no security risks.</dd>
